<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eresburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eresburg was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> hill fort on the site of modern Obermarsberg in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, above the Diemel valley. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> captured it in 772 at the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxon-wars">Saxon Wars</a> and destroyed the nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irminsul">Irminsul</a>, the Saxons' sacred pillar. It changed hands several times during the wars and became a Frankish stronghold and later the site of a church and town.</p></div>
